# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/chain_hollowstar.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event hs_dreams_begin
# en: The Black Star Dream
title [c0e94a] = 黑星之梦
# en: You dream of the lake from underneath. There is a round door at the bottom, and above the water a star that is not a light but an absence. A voice says your name like it is tasting it. You wake with frost on your pillow.
text [aadef3] = 你梦见从水下仰望湖面。湖底有一扇圆门，水面之上有一颗星——它不是光，而是一种缺失。一个声音念出你的名字，像在品尝它。你醒来时，枕头上结着霜。
# en: A dreamscape: a frozen lake seen from beneath, a round door glowing at the bottom, and above it a star that is a hole in the sky.
scene [ba146d] = 梦境：从水下仰望结冰的湖面，湖底一扇发光的圆门，上方一颗如同天空破洞的星。
# en: Write the dream down
opt.left.label [f34e00] = 把梦记下来
# en: Your notes fill four pages. In the morning you don't remember writing the last line: "It is not asleep. It is waiting."
opt.left.say.1 [5620a5] = 你的笔记写满了四页。早上，你不记得自己写过最后一行：“它没有沉睡。它在等待。”
# en: Ask Seraphine what it means
opt.right.label [37112a] = 问瑟拉芬这是什么意思
# en: Seraphine listens, then hands you a sprig of lavender. "It won't stop the dreams," she says. "But it'll make them smell nicer."
opt.right.say.1 [2b221e] = 瑟拉芬听完，递给你一枝薰衣草。“它止不住那些梦，”她说，“但能让梦闻起来香一点。”

@event hs_grey_stranger
# en: A Man in Grey
title [52d66e] = 灰衣人
# en: Late at night in the courtyard, Kael is arguing with a tall man in a grey coat. The fountain between them has frozen mid-splash. "The door under the lake will be opened," the man says calmly. "By you, or by your sister. Your mother doesn't mind which."
text [4465b8] = 深夜的庭院里，凯尔正和一个穿灰色大衣的高个子男人争执。他们之间的喷泉在水花溅起的一刻冻住了。“湖底那扇门终会被打开，”那人平静地说，“由你，或者由你妹妹。你母亲不在乎是谁。”
# en: A frozen fountain in a moonlit courtyard; a tall man in a grey coat facing a younger man, frost spreading from both.
scene [27f9c8] = 月光下庭院里一座冻结的喷泉；一个穿灰大衣的高个男人与一个年轻人对峙，霜从两人脚下蔓延。
# en: Try to slip away unseen
opt.left.label [fb2449] = 试着悄悄溜走
# en: You back into the shadows. The man in grey turns his head and looks straight at where you're hiding, then smiles and walks away. You don't sleep much.
opt.left.say.1 [e83ac5] = 你退回阴影里。灰衣人转过头，直直地看向你藏身的地方，然后笑了笑，走开了。你一夜没怎么睡。
# en: Step out and interrupt
opt.right.label [ec8045] = 走出去打断他们
# en: "Everything all right?" The man in grey studies you, nods politely and leaves; the cold he leaves behind bites through your sleeves. Kael's hands are shaking. "You shouldn't have done that," he says. "...Thank you."
opt.right.say.1 [36ccb7] = “没事吧？”灰衣人打量了你一番，礼貌地点点头，走了；他留下的寒意透过袖子直往里钻。凯尔的手在发抖。“你不该这么做的，”他说，“……谢谢。”

@event hs_founders_records
# en: The Founders' Ledger
title [92688a] = 创始者账簿
# en: In the archive vault you find the Founders' Ledger, three hundred years old. The entry for the academy's founding year has been cut out with a razor. But the page beneath still holds the impression of the pen.
text [8885d9] = 你在档案库里找到了三百年前的《创始者账簿》。记载学院创立那一年的条目被人用刀片割掉了。但下面那一页上，仍留着笔尖的压痕。
# en: A dusty archive vault, a giant ledger open on a lectern, one page carefully razored out.
scene [f6e330] = 积满灰尘的档案库，讲台上摊开一本巨大的账簿，其中一页被小心地割掉了。
# en: Leave it — this feels dangerous
opt.left.label [7ed54a] = 算了——这感觉很危险
# en: You close the ledger. The dust settles. Some doors are better left alone. Probably.
opt.left.say.1 [cce53b] = 你合上账簿。灰尘落定。有些门最好别去碰。大概吧。
# en: Rub charcoal over the page
opt.right.label [3eeead] = 用炭笔拓印那一页
# en: Ghostly letters emerge: "Seven towers, seven locks. The Star sleeps beneath the water. The key is a star that holds no light." The founders built the academy as a seal.
opt.right.say.1 [8ceb50] = 幽灵般的字迹浮现出来：“七塔七锁。星眠于水下。钥匙是一颗不盛光的星。”创始者建起这座学院，正是为了作一道封印。
# en: The impression is too faint. You make out only three words: "...beneath the water..."
opt.right.say.2 [bee5f6] = 压痕太浅了。你只辨认出四个字：“……于水下……”

@event hs_restricted_founders
# en: The Chained Drafts
title [872dc4] = 锁链里的草稿
# en: The archive's ledger has its founding page cut out. The Restricted Section keeps the founders' own drafts, chained to a shelf at the very back, and the chain is warm to the touch. Somewhere behind you, a book turns its own page.
text [c28920] = 档案库那本账簿里建校的那一页被割掉了。禁书区里藏着创始者们亲笔的草稿，用锁链锁在最里面的书架上，那锁链摸上去是温的。你身后某处，一本书自己翻了一页。
# en: A dark aisle of the Restricted Section at midnight, a bundle of yellowed drafts chained to a shelf, the chain faintly glowing.
scene [1a2ec0] = 午夜禁书区一条昏暗的过道，一捆发黄的草稿被锁链锁在书架上，锁链隐隐发光。
# en: Work the chain loose
opt.left.label [aa3f60] = 把锁链弄松
# en: The links give one by one, and burn your fingers doing it. The drafts say it plainly, in three hands: "Seven towers, seven locks. The Star sleeps beneath the water. The key is a star that holds no light." Lumenhold is a seal.
opt.left.say.1 [9baf12] = 链环一节一节松开，烫伤了你的手指。草稿上用三种笔迹写得明明白白：“七座塔，七把锁。星沉睡于水下。钥匙是一颗不含光的星。”流明堡就是一道封印。
# en: The chain shrieks like a ward. You're out of the window before the prefect arrives, but not before he sees your face. Detention, and a long look from the librarian.
opt.left.say.2 [c540d6] = 锁链像护界一样尖叫起来。你在级长赶到前翻出了窗，但他还是看见了你的脸。禁闭，外加图书管理员长长的一眼。
# en: Copy the shelf-list instead
opt.right.label [e5a618] = 改抄书目清单
# en: The drafts' shelf-list is less guarded and nearly as strange. One entry reads only "Key: the seventh tower, top room. Do not lend." You copy it out by the light of a reading charm you have to keep alive for an hour, and it leaves you drained.
opt.right.say.1 [ba1ef3] = 草稿的书目清单看守得没那么严，却几乎一样古怪。其中一条只写着：“钥匙：第七塔，顶层。不外借。”你借着一道得撑上一个钟头的阅读咒的光把它抄下来，抄完人都虚脱了。

@event hs_boathouse_bell
# en: The Hatch in the Boathouse
title [333304] = 船屋里的活板门
# en: Under a coil of rotten rope in the boathouse there's a hatch, and under the hatch, stone steps going down into the lake. The air coming up smells of cold bronze. From somewhere below, very faint, a bell is tolling under the water.
text [d8dbb2] = 船屋里一卷烂绳子底下有一扇活板门，门下是通往湖里的石阶。往上涌的空气带着冰冷的青铜味。下面某处，非常微弱，一口钟正在水底鸣响。
# en: The inside of an old wooden boathouse at night, a square hatch open in the floorboards, stone steps leading down into dark water.
scene [947bde] = 夜里一座旧木船屋的内部，地板上一扇方形活板门敞开着，石阶通向漆黑的水里。
# en: Go down the steps
opt.left.label [26f409] = 走下台阶
# en: The steps become a tunnel under the lakebed, dry and ice-cold, running toward the sound. You follow it until you can see the bell's green rim in the dark ahead. Then you turn back, frozen to the bone, and remember every turning.
opt.left.say.1 [1ef535] = 台阶变成了湖床下的一条隧道，干燥而冰冷，朝着钟声延伸。你一直走到能看见前方黑暗中那口钟青绿的边沿。然后你转身往回走，冻得透骨，每一个拐弯都记在心里。
# en: The third step is ice. You go into the water to the chest and come up gasping, but you've seen it: a tunnel under the lake, running toward the bell. You walk home soaked.
opt.left.say.2 [c6b05c] = 第三级台阶结了冰。你一下子掉进齐胸深的水里，喘着气爬出来，但你看见了：湖底有条隧道，通向那口钟。你湿淋淋地走回了家。
# en: Listen at the waterline
opt.right.label [8f90c9] = 在水边倾听
# en: You lie on the boards with your ear to the gap. The bell tolls seven times, slow, and between the strokes you hear a draught moving under the lake, the way air moves in a corridor. Something down there is a door. You don't sleep well.
opt.right.say.1 [0754e3] = 你趴在木板上，耳朵贴着缝隙。钟慢慢地敲了七下，在两响之间，你听见湖底有气流在移动，就像空气在走廊里流动那样。下面有一扇门。你一夜没睡好。

@event hs_seraphine_shadow
# en: One Star Too Many
title [bd51fe] = 多出来的一颗星
# en: Seraphine has turned the great telescope down, not at the sky but at the lake, where the stars are reflected. "Look," she says. "In the water. There's one star too many, and it's dark." She counts under her breath. "It wasn't there in my dream. It was in yours."
text [f656d5] = 瑟拉芬把那架大望远镜往下转，没对着天空，而是对着倒映着星星的湖面。“看，”她说，“水里。多了一颗星，而且是暗的。”她低声数着。“我的梦里没有它。是你的梦里有。”
# en: An observatory at night, the great telescope tilted down toward the window and the lake below, a seer pointing at the reflection of the stars in the water.
scene [93fed0] = 夜里的观星台，大望远镜朝下对着窗外的湖，一位预言者指着水中星星的倒影。
# en: Chart it with her
opt.left.label [c4492b] = 和她一起绘出它的位置
# en: You chart it till dawn on the cold floor: a small dark shape in the reflection that has no star above it, sitting exactly over the middle of the lake. Your knees never quite forgive you.
opt.left.say.1 [ff1233] = 你们在冰冷的地板上一直画到天亮：倒影里有一个小小的暗影，上方的天空里却没有对应的星，它正好停在湖的正中央。你的膝盖再也没完全原谅你。
# en: Tell her about your dream
opt.right.label [cc1d2c] = 告诉她你的梦
# en: She finishes your sentences, three of them, before you've started them. Then she shows you the dark star in the water, right over the middle of the lake. You both stop talking for a long time.
opt.right.say.1 [167dc3] = 你还没开口，她就替你说完了三句话。然后她指给你看水中那颗暗星，正在湖心上方。你们俩很久都没再说话。

@event hs_kael_truth
# en: What Kael Is Running From
title [5fe24d] = 凯尔在逃避什么
# en: Kael sits with you on the boathouse jetty. "My family serve something under this lake," he says at last. "They sent me here to open its door. I came to stop them. Some nights I'm not sure which I'll actually do."
text [01cf3e] = 凯尔和你一起坐在船屋的栈桥上。“我的家族侍奉着这湖底的某样东西，”他终于开口，“他们派我来打开它的门。我来是为了阻止他们。有些夜里，我也不确定自己最后会做哪一件。”
# en: Two students sitting on the edge of the frozen boathouse jetty at night, one with frost in his hair, both looking down at the black water.
scene [ede058] = 夜里两个学生坐在结冰的船屋栈桥边缘，其中一人发间挂着霜，两人都低头看着漆黑的湖水。
# en: "Then we stop them together."
opt.left.label [72f262] = “那我们一起阻止他们。”
# en: He looks at you for a long moment, and the frost on the jetty melts a little. "Together," he repeats, as if trying out a word from another language.
opt.left.say.1 [734531] = 他久久地看着你，栈桥上的霜融化了一点。“一起。”他重复道，像在尝试一个外语单词。
# en: Tell the headmistress
opt.right.label [bcf093] = 告诉院长
# en: The headmistress thanks you gravely. The next day Kael is moved to a room in the headmistress's tower. He doesn't look at you anymore.
opt.right.say.1 [07e3f1] = 院长郑重地感谢了你。第二天，凯尔被搬进了院长塔楼里的一个房间。他再也不看你了。

@event hs_star_mark
# en: The Cold Coin Burns
title [2ace55] = 冰冷的硬币在灼烧
# en: The black-starred relic you've been carrying burns suddenly, so cold it feels hot. When you drop it, there's a pale star-shaped mark on your palm. It hums when you're near the lake.
text [32d3ff] = 你一直带在身上的那件黑星遗物突然灼烧起来，冷到像是滚烫。你把它扔下时，掌心多了一枚苍白的星形印记。靠近湖边时，它会嗡嗡作响。
# en: A student's open palm, a pale star-shaped mark glowing on it, a blackened coin smoking on the floor beside them.
scene [be9e03] = 一个学生摊开的掌心，上面闪着苍白的星形印记，一枚发黑的硬币在旁边的地上冒着烟。
# en: Throw the relic into the lake
opt.left.label [9e07e3] = 把遗物扔进湖里
# en: It sinks without a ripple. The mark on your hand fades — almost entirely. Something under the water sighs.
opt.left.say.1 [f57ba3] = 它沉了下去，没起一丝涟漪。你手上的印记褪去了——几乎完全褪去。水下有什么东西叹了口气。
# en: Keep it. Feel the power.
opt.right.label [9c18f9] = 留着它。感受这份力量。
# en: The mark pulses with every heartbeat. Spells come easier now. Much easier. That should probably worry you more than it does.
opt.right.say.1 [49d379] = 印记随着每一次心跳搏动。现在施法容易多了。容易太多了。这本该比现在更让你担心才对。

@event hs_grey_offer
# en: An Offer in Grey
title [72fb9a] = 灰色的提议
# en: The man in grey is waiting at your library table. "You've been asking questions about the Star," he says pleasantly. "It's noticed you. It could make you extraordinary. All it wants is for someone to open a door."
text [8e2f80] = 灰衣人正等在你的图书馆座位上。“你一直在打听那颗星，”他和颜悦色地说，“它注意到你了。它能让你非同凡响。它想要的，只是有人去打开一扇门。”
# en: A grey-coated man sitting uninvited at a library table, a black velvet box open in front of him, the candles around him burning blue.
scene [252bba] = 一个穿灰大衣的男人不请自来地坐在图书馆桌旁，面前打开着一只黑丝绒盒子，周围的蜡烛燃着蓝色火焰。
# en: "Get out."
opt.left.label [f967c3] = “滚出去。”
# en: He inclines his head and leaves. The candles return to yellow. You realise your hands are trembling.
opt.left.say.1 [0a3723] = 他欠了欠身，离开了。蜡烛恢复了黄色。你这才发现自己的手在发抖。
# en: "...What would it give me?"
opt.right.label [d466af] = “……它能给我什么？”
# en: He shows you, just for a moment. Power, endless and cold. When he's gone, you can still taste it.
opt.right.say.1 [5c20e2] = 他给你看了，只有一瞬间。力量，无穷无尽，冰冷彻骨。他走后，你仍能尝到那股滋味。

@event hs_grey_invitation
# en: A Seat at the Northern Table
title [c52641] = 北境之席
# en: There is a letter on your pillow, sealed with a black star. The handwriting is beautiful. "The families have watched you with great interest," it says. "There is a seat for you at our table, when the door is opened. Come to the boathouse at midnight, or burn this. Either is an answer."
text [13f2ac] = 你的枕头上放着一封信，用一枚黑色的星封着蜡。字迹很漂亮。“世家怀着极大的兴趣关注着你，”信上写道，“门打开之时，我们的席上会有你一个座位。午夜到船屋来，或者烧了这封信。两者都是答复。”
# en: A black-edged letter on a dormitory pillow, its wax seal pressed with a star that has no light in it.
scene [f56301] = 宿舍枕头上一封镶黑边的信，封蜡上压着一颗不发光的星。
# en: Go to the boathouse
opt.left.label [526aa1] = 去船屋
# en: The man in grey is waiting with two cups of something hot. He talks to you as an equal for an hour. You come back with frost in your hair and the feeling of having been measured, and found to fit.
opt.left.say.1 [c84e12] = 灰衣人端着两杯热饮在等你。他像对待平辈一样和你谈了一个小时。你回来时头发上沾着霜，觉得自己被丈量过，而且尺寸正合适。
# en: Burn it
opt.right.label [162285] = 烧掉它
# en: The paper burns blue and slow, and smells of the lake. It takes a long time to go out. Climbing back from where you've been is slower still, but this is a step.
opt.right.say.1 [dfcc08] = 信纸燃起蓝色的火，烧得很慢，散发着湖水的气味。它很久才烧尽。从你走到的地方爬回来还要更慢，但这是一步。

@event hs_grey_tests
# en: The Good Argument
title [e22d78] = 好听的道理
# en: The man in grey falls into step beside you outside the infirmary. "You help people," he says pleasantly. "I admire it. But think how many more you could help with real power. The Star doesn't care what it's used for. Only that someone uses it."
text [9adfef] = 灰衣人在医务室外与你并肩而行。“你帮助别人，”他和气地说，“我很欣赏。可想想看，若有真正的力量，你能多帮多少人。星不在乎它被用来做什么，只在乎有人用它。”
# en: A grey-coated man standing beside a student at the infirmary window, both looking down at a first-year with a bandaged arm.
scene [86ebbc] = 一个穿灰外套的男人和一名学生并肩站在医务室窗前，一起低头看着一个手臂缠着绷带的一年级生。
# en: "No."
opt.left.label [371a7a] = “不。”
# en: "No," you say. He smiles as if you'd said something charming, and leaves. The first-year in the window waves at you. You wave back, and your hand is shaking.
opt.left.say.1 [ce8c7e] = “不，”你说。他笑了笑，仿佛你说了句讨人喜欢的话，然后离开了。窗边的一年级生朝你挥手。你也挥手，手在发抖。
# en: "...How many more?"
opt.right.label [faa864] = “……能多帮多少？”
# en: He tells you. The numbers are very large and very cold. That night, you dream of the lake from underneath, and you are not frightened in the dream.
opt.right.say.1 [3239c8] = 他告诉了你。那些数字非常大，也非常冷。那天夜里，你梦见从湖底往上看，而梦里的你并不害怕。

@event hs_wardens_notice
# en: The Headmistress Takes Note
title [f7baa8] = 院长记下了你
# en: On the grand stair the headmistress stops beside you. "Several people have told me about you," she says, "and not one of them was complaining. That is rare." Her silver ring catches the light. "I keep a list of students I would trust with a door. Don't let it go to your head."
text [aef554] = 在大楼梯上，院长在你身旁停下。“好几个人跟我提起过你，”她说，“没有一个是来告状的。这很少见。”她的银戒指映着光。“我有一份名单，上面是我愿意托付一扇门的学生。别因此得意忘形。”
# en: A tall woman in dark robes pausing on a stair to look down at one student among many, a silver ring glinting on her hand.
scene [25a5bf] = 一位身着深色长袍的高个女人在楼梯上停步，低头看着众多学生中的一个，手上的银戒指闪着光。
# en: "I'd be honoured."
opt.left.label [bec864] = “我深感荣幸。”
# en: "Good," she says. "Honour is a heavy thing to carry. Practise." She walks on. You stand on the stair for some time.
opt.left.say.1 [e74b53] = “很好，”她说，“荣誉是件沉重的东西。多练练。”她继续往前走。你在楼梯上站了好一会儿。
# en: "What kind of door?"
opt.right.label [ee5679] = “什么样的门？”
# en: Her short, delighted laugh. "The kind that ought to stay shut," she says. "Keep asking questions like that. Just not on the stairs."
opt.right.say.1 [c568f6] = 她发出那声短促而愉快的笑。“应该一直关着的那种，”她说，“继续问这样的问题吧。只是别在楼梯上问。”

@event hs_seventh_tower
# en: The Seventh Tower
title [44b8dc] = 第七塔
# en: The seventh tower has been locked for a century. You find a way in. At the very top, a single room: dust, moonlight, and a star-shaped hollow in the wall, holding something that does not reflect any light.
text [9081b5] = 第七塔已经锁了一个世纪。你找到了进去的路。塔顶只有一个房间：灰尘、月光，墙上一个星形的凹槽，里面放着某样不反射任何光的东西。
# en: The top of a narrow, abandoned tower, cobwebbed and moonlit, with a wall bearing a star-shaped recess.
scene [c775ba] = 一座狭窄废塔的顶层，蛛网密布，月光洒入，墙上有一个星形凹槽。
# en: Take it quietly
opt.left.label [2a0b10] = 悄悄拿走
# en: A key shaped like a star, black as a hole in the world. As you lift it, every candle in the academy goes out for one breath. You walk back in the dark with it cold against your ribs, and you don't sleep.
opt.left.say.1 [f9b295] = 一把星形的钥匙，黑得像世界上的一个洞。你拿起它的一刻，学院里每一支蜡烛都熄灭了一口气的工夫。你揣着它在黑暗中走回去，它冰冷地贴着你的肋骨，你一夜没睡。
# en: A ward shrieks. A prefect finds you on the stairs. You get detention and a very long look from the headmistress.
opt.left.say.2 [ca0973] = 防护咒尖叫起来。一位级长在楼梯上逮住了你。你被关了禁闭，还挨了院长很长很长的一眼。
# en: Take it boldly
opt.right.label [f86c9d] = 强行拿走
# en: You tear through the ward with brute force, and it drains you to the bone. The key comes free. Every candle in the academy goes out for one breath, and somewhere below, a door hears it.
opt.right.say.1 [777369] = 你凭蛮力撕开了护界，这把你耗得精疲力尽。钥匙脱落下来。学院里每一支蜡烛都熄灭了一口气的工夫，而在下面某处，一扇门听见了。
# en: The ward throws you down two flights of stairs.
opt.right.say.2 [1014e6] = 防护咒把你甩下了两层楼梯。

@event hs_key_breakfast
# en: Something of Mine
title [f9fe6f] = 我的东西
# en: At breakfast the headmistress sets down her cup and looks straight at you along the whole length of the hall. Afterwards she is waiting at the door. "Every candle in my academy went out," she says pleasantly, "and you have something of mine."
text [e0137d] = 早餐时，校长放下杯子，隔着整个大厅直直地看着你。之后她在门口等你。“我学院里的每一支蜡烛都灭了，”她愉快地说，“而你拿着我的一样东西。”
# en: The high table at breakfast, the headmistress setting down her cup and looking along the hall at one student, the candles behind her newly lit.
scene [fdadd9] = 早餐时的高桌，校长放下杯子，沿着大厅望向一名学生，她身后的蜡烛刚刚重新点亮。
# en: Give her the key
opt.left.label [28b877] = 把钥匙交给她
# en: She takes it in a gloved hand without looking at it. "Thank you. It will be where it is needed, on the night. So, I hope, will you." You feel lighter, and a little robbed.
opt.left.say.1 [86a9c7] = 她用戴手套的手接过去，看都没看一眼。“谢谢。那一夜，它会在需要它的地方。我希望你也会。”你觉得轻松了些，又有点像被抢了。
# en: Keep it
opt.right.label [87c2f5] = 留着它
# en: A long pause. "Then keep it close," she says, "and never let it near the water before its time. People will come asking for it. Not all of them will ask." From then on, the man in grey always seems to know where you are.
opt.right.say.1 [d35dc1] = 长长的停顿。“那就贴身收好，”她说，“时候未到，绝不要让它靠近湖水。会有人来讨要它。不是每个人都会开口讨。”从那以后，灰衣人似乎总知道你在哪儿。

@event hs_isolde_summons
# en: The Headmistress Knows
title [214bdc] = 院长知道了
# en: The headmistress summons you to her tower. "You have been following the same thread I have," she says. "On the night of the Blossom moon, the seal will weaken. I need people I can trust beneath the lake. Or you can walk away. No one would blame you."
text [aa0d92] = 院长把你召进她的塔楼。“你一直在追寻和我同一条线索，”她说，“花潮之月那一夜，封印会减弱。我需要可以信任的人到湖底去。你也可以选择离开。没有人会怪你。”
# en: A circular study at the top of a tower, walls lined with sleeping portraits, the headmistress standing by a window that looks down on the lake.
scene [8d69ed] = 塔顶的圆形书房，墙上挂满沉睡的肖像，院长站在俯瞰湖面的窗前。
# en: Walk away
opt.left.label [96da1a] = 离开
# en: "Wise," she says, and you can't tell if she means it. "Then stay above, and keep the first-years indoors."
opt.left.say.1 [00df9c] = “明智。”她说，你分不清她是不是真心的。“那就留在上面，让一年级生待在屋里。”
# en: "I'll be there."
opt.right.label [d06338] = “我会去的。”
# en: She presses a silver ward-ring into your hand. "{flag(star_key): The founders' key is with you. Keep it close.|{flag(gave_star_key): The founders' key is in my desk.|The founders' key is kept at the top of the seventh tower.}} On the night, it comes down with us. Learn quickly. You have until Blossomtide." You lose a little sleep over that every night.
opt.right.say.1 [76415e] = 她把一枚银色的守护戒指按进你手心。“{flag(star_key): 创始者的钥匙在你身上。收好。|{flag(gave_star_key): 创始者的钥匙在我的书桌里。|创始者的钥匙藏在第七塔塔顶。}}那一夜，它会跟我们一起下去。学快点。你只有到花潮月为止的时间。”每天夜里，你都为这事少睡一会儿。

@event hs_the_night
# en: The Night the Lake Froze
title [6f7fcc] = 湖面冰封之夜
# en: In the middle of spring, the lake freezes in a single breath. Cracks glow beneath the ice. The bell under the water is tolling, and every candle in the academy leans toward the shore.
text [9423a3] = 正值春天，湖面却在一口气之间冻结了。冰下的裂缝发着光。湖底的钟在敲响，学院里每一支蜡烛都朝着湖岸倾斜。
# en: The whole lake frozen white in the middle of spring, cracks glowing from beneath, students crowding the towers' windows.
scene [b58de9] = 春日里整个湖面冻得雪白，冰下裂缝透出光芒，学生们挤在塔楼的窗前。
# en: Go down beneath the lake
opt.left.label [983634] = 潜入湖底
# en: You run for the boathouse. Behind you, someone is shouting your name. You don't stop.
opt.left.say.1 [28f348] = 你朝船屋奔去。身后有人在喊你的名字。你没有停下。
# en: Stay above and protect the students
opt.right.label [3d4500] = 留在上面保护学生
# en: You hold the doors of the first-year tower all night against things made of frost and whispers. By dawn the lake thaws. Something below is still asleep — for now.
opt.right.say.1 [cee4e5] = 你整夜守着一年级塔楼的大门，抵挡由冰霜与低语构成的东西。黎明时湖面解冻了。下面的那个东西仍在沉睡——暂时。

@event hs_tunnel
# en: The Man in the Tunnel
title [809d66] = 隧道里的人
# en: The tunnel from the boathouse runs down under the ice, slick and glowing blue. Halfway down, the man in grey is waiting{=flag(ilse_taken) and ", and Ilse stands beside him with her eyes on nothing" or ", alone, as if he has all night"}. "Go back up," he says pleasantly. "This isn't your door."
text [0bcdbe] = 从船屋出发的隧道一路向下，钻到冰层底下，湿滑而泛着蓝光。走到一半，灰衣人正等在那里{=flag(ilse_taken) and "，伊尔泽站在他身边，目光空洞" or "，独自一人，仿佛他有整夜的时间"}。“回上面去吧，”他愉快地说，“这不是你的门。”
# en: A slick stone tunnel under the ice, lit blue from above, a tall man in a grey coat standing in the middle of it with his hands folded.
scene [07762c] = 冰层下一条湿滑的石隧道，上方透下蓝光，一个穿灰大衣的高个男人双手交握，站在隧道中间。
# en: Break through him
opt.fight.label [07b59f] = 从他身上闯过去
# en: Combat. Easier with Kael at your side.
opt.fight.hint [fe2cd0] = 战斗。有凯尔在身边会更容易。
# en: Kael's frost and your spell hit him together. He slides back along the ice, bows, and is simply not there any more. You go on with bruised ribs and a clear road.
opt.fight.say.1 [ffdeff] = 凯尔的寒霜和你的咒语同时击中了他。他沿着冰面滑了出去，鞠了一躬，然后就不在那儿了。你带着青肿的肋骨走上畅通的路。
# en: He swats the two of you aside like moths, then steps back to let you pass, smiling. "Go on, then." You go down bleeding, and late.
opt.fight.say.2 [7290b7] = 他像拍飞蛾一样把你们俩扫到一边，然后退开让你们过去，微笑着说：“那就去吧。”你流着血下去，晚了一步。
# en: Your spell catches him square, and he slides back along the ice, surprised for the first time. He bows and is gone. You go on with bruised ribs and a clear road.
opt.fight.say.3 [d1e5ad] = 你的咒语正中他胸口，他沿着冰面滑了出去，第一次露出了意外的神情。他鞠了一躬，消失了。你带着青肿的肋骨走上畅通的路。
# en: He swats your spell aside, then steps back to let you pass, smiling. "Go on, then." You go down bleeding, and late.
opt.fight.say.4 [4f4f17] = 他把你的咒语拍到一边，然后退开让你过去，微笑着说：“那就去吧。”你流着血下去，晚了一步。
# en: Talk your way past
opt.talk.label [f5bc3b] = 说服他让路
# en: Charm. Easier if Ilse is safe, or you know what she was raised for.
opt.talk.hint [ac568b] = 魅力。如果伊尔泽平安，或者你知道她被养大的目的，会更容易。
# en: You tell him the Dumont children have chosen, both of them, and that you know exactly what they were raised for. For a moment he looks old. Then he steps aside. It costs you something to see that look.
opt.talk.say.1 [086c71] = 你告诉他，杜蒙家的两个孩子都已经做了选择，而你清清楚楚地知道他们被养大是为了什么。有那么一刻，他显得苍老了。然后他让开了。看见那副神情，你心里也付出了点什么。
# en: He listens courteously, agrees with every word, and lets you pass only once you've heard every word of his. You arrive shaken, and late.
opt.talk.say.2 [631e3a] = 他彬彬有礼地听着，句句都表示赞同，直到你把他要说的每一句都听完，才放你过去。你到达时心神不宁，也晚了。
# en: You talk fast and well, and somewhere in it he decides you're more trouble than you're worth. He steps aside with a little bow. Your hands don't stop shaking for a while.
opt.talk.say.3 [30715a] = 你说得又快又好，说着说着他认定你麻烦得不值得。他微微鞠躬让开了。你的手抖了好一阵才停。
# en: He listens courteously, agrees with every word, and lets you pass only once you've heard every word of his. You arrive shaken, and late.
opt.talk.say.4 [631e3a] = 他彬彬有礼地听着，句句都表示赞同，直到你把他要说的每一句都听完，才放你过去。你到达时心神不宁，也晚了。
# en: Find another way down
opt.slip.label [1e4f9e] = 另找一条路下去
# en: Guile. Easier if you know the old tunnels.
opt.slip.hint [e07b2c] = 诡计。如果你熟悉那些旧隧道，会更容易。
# en: You know a side passage he doesn't, the one the bell's rope once ran through. You come out below him, breathless and spent, and he never sees you go.
opt.slip.say.1 [c75c91] = 你知道一条他不知道的岔道，就是当年钟绳穿过的那条。你从他下方钻了出来，气喘吁吁、精疲力尽，而他根本没看见你走过。
# en: The side passage is half flooded. You come out soaked and freezing, below him, but late, and he calls a polite good evening after you.
opt.slip.say.2 [705c25] = 岔道一半被水淹了。你从他下方钻出来，浑身湿透、冻得发抖，但晚了一步，他还在你身后客气地道了声晚安。
# en: You fold yourself into the dark and go round him along the wall, a breath at a time. It drains you, but he never turns his head.
opt.slip.say.3 [70ef4d] = 你把自己折进黑暗里，贴着墙一口气一口气地绕过他。这让你精疲力尽，但他始终没有转头。
# en: He turns his head the moment you move. "Good evening." He lets you pass anyway, and the cold he leaves in your bones comes with you.
opt.slip.say.4 [e287c0] = 你一动，他就转过了头。“晚上好。”他还是放你过去了，而他留在你骨头里的寒意也跟着你下去了。

@event hs_threshold
# en: The Founders' Words
title [5a0a8c] = 创始者的咒文
# en: The tunnel ends at a wall of black stone carved with the founders' words, in a script that drifts when you look away. Behind it the bell is tolling. The wall will open for someone who can read it, or someone who can make it.
text [bc4d6a] = 隧道尽头是一面黑石墙，上面刻着创始者的咒文，字迹在你移开目光时会悄悄漂移。墙后，钟声在响。这面墙会为能读懂它的人打开，或者为能逼它打开的人打开。
# en: A wall of black stone at the end of a tunnel, carved with lines of script that drift when not looked at, a faint bell-tone hanging in the air.
scene [f06531] = 隧道尽头的一面黑石墙，刻着一行行不被注视时就会漂移的字，空气中悬着一丝微弱的钟声。
# en: Read the founders' words
opt.read.label [78313a] = 念出创始者的咒文
# en: Lore. The founders' seal and the seven locks make it easier.
opt.read.hint [4b99a5] = 学识。知道创始者的封印和七把锁会更容易。
# en: You've read these words before, in pieces, and you know where the locks fall. Said whole, they open the wall like a door, and the strain of it sits behind your eyes.
opt.read.say.1 [66592f] = 这些字你以前零零碎碎读到过，也知道那几把锁落在哪里。一口气念完，墙像门一样打开了，那股吃力的劲儿压在你眼睛后面。
# en: You stumble on the last line, and the wall opens only a crack. You squeeze through it; it scrapes skin off your shoulder on the way.
opt.read.say.2 [9a802e] = 你在最后一行卡住了，墙只开了一道缝。你从缝里挤过去，肩膀上被刮掉了一层皮。
# en: You know enough to guess the rest. The wall listens, and slides aside, and the strain of it sits behind your eyes.
opt.read.say.3 [d417b9] = 你知道的足够猜出其余部分。墙听着，滑向一边，那股吃力的劲儿压在你眼睛后面。
# en: You stumble on the last line, and the wall opens only a crack. You squeeze through it; it scrapes skin off your shoulder on the way.
opt.read.say.4 [9a802e] = 你在最后一行卡住了，墙只开了一道缝。你从缝里挤过去，肩膀上被刮掉了一层皮。
# en: You don't know the words, but you know how words like these are built. Line by line, the wall gives way, and the strain of it sits behind your eyes.
opt.read.say.5 [8d1233] = 你不认识这些字，但你知道这样的字是怎么构成的。一行一行地，墙让开了，那股吃力的劲儿压在你眼睛后面。
# en: The script slides away from you. In the end the wall opens a crack on its own, as if amused. You squeeze through; it takes skin with it.
opt.read.say.6 [b9d435] = 那些字从你眼前溜走。最后墙自己开了一道缝，像是觉得好笑。你挤了过去，它带走了你一层皮。
# en: Force the stone open
opt.force.label [da75b6] = 强行打开石墙
# en: Arcana, and it hurts. Easier if Maud taught you her wards.
opt.force.hint [4dd1c8] = 奥术，而且会疼。如果莫德教过你她的护界，会更容易。
# en: You trace Maud's wards backwards into the stone, the way she showed you. The wall cracks down the middle and opens, and your hands ache to the elbow.
opt.force.say.1 [8407a2] = 你照莫德教你的那样，把她的护界反着描进石头里。墙从中间裂开，打开了，你的双手一直疼到手肘。
# en: The stone fights back. You get through in the end, but your hands are raw and shaking.
opt.force.say.2 [2e5d18] = 石头在反抗。你最后还是过去了，但双手血肉模糊，抖个不停。
# en: You put everything you have into the stone, and it cracks down the middle. Your hands ache to the elbow.
opt.force.say.3 [8e17f7] = 你把全部力量都压进石头里，它从中间裂开了。你的双手一直疼到手肘。
# en: The stone fights back. You get through in the end, but your hands are raw and shaking.
opt.force.say.4 [2e5d18] = 石头在反抗。你最后还是过去了，但双手血肉模糊，抖个不停。

@event hs_beneath
# en: The Door Beneath the Lake
title [76c2d3] = 湖底之门
# en: Beyond the wall, the round door. It stands open a crack. Through it, the Hollow Star looks at you — and it is beautiful, and it is hungry, and it knows your name.{=flag(kael_ally) and " Kael is beside you, wand raised, frost spreading from his feet." or ""}
text [c4b228] = 墙后就是那扇圆门。它开着一道缝。透过门缝，空洞之星在看着你——它很美，它很饥饿，它知道你的名字。{=flag(kael_ally) and "凯尔就在你身旁，魔杖高举，冰霜从他脚下蔓延开来。" or ""}
# en: A vast domed cavern under the lake, a round door of black stone standing open a crack, and through it a star that is pure absence.
scene [d3244b] = 湖底一座巨大的穹形洞窟，一扇黑石圆门开着一道缝，门后是一颗纯粹由“缺失”构成的星。
# en: Seal the door
opt.seal.label [b5b84d] = 封印这扇门
# en: Needs the star key, the founders' secret or a ward-ring. Arcana; preparation and the way down make it easier. It can fail.
opt.seal.hint [1129af] = 需要星钥、创始者的秘密或一枚守护戒指。奥术；准备和下来的路走得越顺越容易。可能失败。
# en: {flag(knows_founders_seal): You speak the founders' words|You set the seal with everything you have}, and the door grinds shut. The Star screams without sound. Above, the ice cracks and the lake breathes again.
opt.seal.say.1 [894b56] = {flag(knows_founders_seal): 你念出创始者的咒文|你倾尽所有设下封印}，门轰隆隆地合上了。星无声地尖叫。上方，冰层碎裂，湖重新开始呼吸。
# en: Your seal falters. Kael throws every ounce of frost in him into it, and it still isn't enough: the door stays ajar. The last thing you see is the headmistress's lantern coming down the tunnel.
opt.seal.say.2 [69a006] = 你的封印动摇了。凯尔把体内每一分寒冰都押了上去，仍然不够：门依旧半开着。你看见的最后一样东西，是校长的提灯沿着隧道下来。
# en: Your seal falters and breaks, and takes most of you with it. The door stays ajar. The last thing you see is the headmistress's lantern coming down the tunnel.
opt.seal.say.3 [c2675b] = 你的封印动摇、碎裂，几乎带走了你的全部。门依旧半开着。你看见的最后一样东西，是校长的提灯沿着隧道下来。
# en: {flag(knows_founders_seal): You speak the founders' words|You set the seal with everything you have}, and the door grinds shut. The Star screams without sound. Above, the ice cracks and the lake breathes again.
opt.seal.say.4 [894b56] = {flag(knows_founders_seal): 你念出创始者的咒文|你倾尽所有设下封印}，门轰隆隆地合上了。星无声地尖叫。上方，冰层碎裂，湖重新开始呼吸。
# en: Your seal falters. Kael throws every ounce of frost in him into it, and it still isn't enough: the door stays ajar. The last thing you see is the headmistress's lantern coming down the tunnel.
opt.seal.say.5 [69a006] = 你的封印动摇了。凯尔把体内每一分寒冰都押了上去，仍然不够：门依旧半开着。你看见的最后一样东西，是校长的提灯沿着隧道下来。
# en: Your seal falters and breaks, and takes most of you with it. The door stays ajar. The last thing you see is the headmistress's lantern coming down the tunnel.
opt.seal.say.6 [c2675b] = 你的封印动摇、碎裂，几乎带走了你的全部。门依旧半开着。你看见的最后一样东西，是校长的提灯沿着隧道下来。
# en: {flag(knows_founders_seal): You speak the founders' words|You set the seal with everything you have}, and the door grinds shut. The Star screams without sound. Above, the ice cracks and the lake breathes again.
opt.seal.say.7 [894b56] = {flag(knows_founders_seal): 你念出创始者的咒文|你倾尽所有设下封印}，门轰隆隆地合上了。星无声地尖叫。上方，冰层碎裂，湖重新开始呼吸。
# en: Your seal falters. Kael throws every ounce of frost in him into it, and it still isn't enough: the door stays ajar. The last thing you see is the headmistress's lantern coming down the tunnel.
opt.seal.say.8 [69a006] = 你的封印动摇了。凯尔把体内每一分寒冰都押了上去，仍然不够：门依旧半开着。你看见的最后一样东西，是校长的提灯沿着隧道下来。
# en: Your seal falters and breaks, and takes most of you with it. The door stays ajar. The last thing you see is the headmistress's lantern coming down the tunnel.
